The knockout stage of the [[2026 AFA World Cup]] began on 26 June 2026. The top two teams from each of the twelve groups advanced to the knockout stage, with the eight best group winners receiving byes to the round of 16. The remaining four group winners and all twelve runners-up competed in a preliminary knockout round.

