==== Match 1: Aetolia 0–2 Sanrobonia ====
[[Sanrobonia national football team|Sanrobonia]] comfortably advanced past [[Aetolia national football team|Aetolia]] in [[Castejón]], scoring in the 15th and 60th minutes to seal a 2–0 win. The co-host never looked troubled, controlling possession throughout and limiting Aetolia to few chances.

==== Match 2: Okaiken 1–2 Ayorin ====
[[Ayorin national football team|Ayorin]] pulled off a dramatic upset in [[Yerba Buena]], knocking out [[Okaiken national football team|Okaiken]] with a stoppage-time winner. [[Kenzo Sato]] had given Okaiken the lead in the 42nd minute, and they looked set to advance until Ayorin equalised in the 60th minute. With the match heading for a draw, Ayorin struck in the first minute of stoppage time to seal a famous 2–1 victory.

==== Match 3: Zong 2–0 Sinchew ====
[[Zong national football team|Zong]] eased past [[Sinchew national football team|Sinchew]] in [[Martapura]], scoring twice in seven minutes just before half-time. Goals in the 30th and 37th minutes proved enough, as Zong controlled the match and Sinchew rarely threatened.

==== Match 4: Orma 2–0 Sanyan ====
[[Orma national football team|Orma]] dominated [[Sanyan national football team|Sanyan]] in [[Telukuba]], with [[Mikael Dirra]] opening the scoring in the 21st minute and [[Yohannes Goba]] adding a second five minutes after the break. Orma controlled possession throughout and Sanyan never seriously threatened.

